2026-11-12T00:25:35.257-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="525107e5-fd90-4b39-81f6-503822000347" status="approved" answer="The CI pipeline would detect a vulnerable `pyyaml` dependency by first running a vulnerability scan (e.g., using Snyk, Dependabot, or a similar tool) that checks all project dependencies against known vulnerabilities. Specifically, it would identify if `pyyaml` is installed at a version below 5.4, as this is the affected range for the critical vulnerability CVE-2020-14343 (arbitrary code execution via untrusted YAML parsing). The pipeline would then explicitly verify that no vulnerable `pyyaml` versions exist in the project. If the scan confirms the project still uses `pyyaml < 5.4`, the pipeline would immediately fail the build, preventing deployment. This ensures compliance with the critical severity requirement and avoids exploitation of the unpatched vulnerability. The check directly aligns with the advisory (s0036_rel id 20077), which mandates fixing to version 5.4 or higher. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-04 (s0036_rel id 20077): pyyaml affected < 5.4, severity critical. CVE-2020-14343: Arbitrary code execution when untrusted YAML is parsed with full_load or FullLoader. Fixed in 5.4."
