2026-11-12T00:29:05.929-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="aa9835ee-6fc5-4ea4-accc-06477a53dcab" status="approved" answer="Based on your plan and the provided facts, patch all services immediately. The vulnerability (CVE-2023-0842) affects all services using xml2js versions < 0.5.0 with medium severity. Since the facts specify no service-specific business impact or exposure details, we cannot prioritize individual services. The critical action is universal: update all xml2js instances to version 0.5.0 or later to resolve the prototype pollution risk. Without additional data on which services are publicly exposed or critical to operations, the highest risk is mitigated by patching all affected services simultaneously. This aligns with the vulnerability's severity and the fixed version. Delaying patching any service risks exploitation via the __proto__ key in parsed XML, potentially causing prototype pollution. Prioritize this update across all services to ensure consistent security posture without further delay. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-17 (s0036_rel id 20090): xml2js affected < 0.5.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-0842: Prototype pollution through the __proto__ key in parsed XML. Fixed in 0.5.0."
