2026-11-12T01:00:04.611-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="0bae3903-bb34-4c45-b56e-4781575db7ea" status="approved" answer="Based on the provided facts, all services using `ws` >=8.0.0 and <8.17.1 are equally vulnerable to CVE-2024-37890 (high severity). This vulnerability allows denial of service via excessive request headers. The fix requires upgrading to `ws@8.17.1`.  \n\nSince the advisory specifies no service-specific business impact data, **prioritize patching all services simultaneously**. The vulnerability\u2019s criticality (high) and identical exposure across services mean no single service has higher risk than others. Delaying patching any service risks DoS attacks, as the vulnerability affects all `ws` versions in the affected range.  \n\nPer your plan, while business impact evaluation is ideal, the absence of service-specific details here necessitates immediate uniform patching to `ws@8.17.1` for all services. This minimizes risk without assuming differential impact. Do not delay\u2014patching all services to the fixed version resolves the vulnerability consistently and urgently. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-10 (s0036_rel id 20083): ws affected >= 8.0.0, < 8.17.1, severity high. CVE-2024-37890: Denial of service from a request whose header count exceeds server.maxHeadersCount. Fixed in 8.17.1."
2026-11-12T01:00:04.627-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="0bae3903-bb34-4c45-b56e-4781575db7ea" partition=0 offset=326
