2026-11-12T01:17:21.932-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="fd76d8b8-44f2-459b-91c7-3d943e6fd747" status="approved" answer="To mitigate CVE-2023-44487 (HTTP/2 rapid reset DoS) until golang.org/x/net upgrades past the fix, implement these compensating controls per your plan:  \n\n1. **Enforce version constraints**: Explicitly require `golang.org/x/net >= 0.17.0` in dependency management (e.g., `go.mod`), excluding all versions `< 0.17.0` as per VULN-0036-HW9-19 (s0036_rel id 20092).  \n\n2. **Implement runtime checks**: Add pre-execution validation to block operations if the vulnerable version is detected (e.g., via `go version` checks in CI/CD pipelines or application startup scripts). This prevents vulnerable HTTP/2 interactions until the fix is applied.  \n\n3. **Monitor fixed version availability**: Track `golang.org/x/net@v0.17.0` release channels (e.g., GitHub releases) to trigger timely upgrades once the patched version is stable and compatible.  \n\nThese steps ensure immediate protection against the high-severity vulnerability while aligning with the advisory\u2019s affected versions and fix. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-19 (s0036_rel id 20092): golang.org/x/net affected < 0.17.0, severity high. CVE-2023-44487: HTTP/2 rapid reset denial of service. Fixed in 0.17.0."
