2026-11-12T01:32:33.361-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="34270bd6-f35b-4dc8-9ad7-cec37c03cb39" status="approved" answer="A CI pipeline detects vulnerable jinja2 dependencies by first running a dependency vulnerability scan (e.g., using Snyk or Trivy). The scan identifies jinja2 versions below 3.1.3 as affected by the medium-severity vulnerability CVE-2024-22195 (Cross-site scripting via xmlattr filter), per advisory VULN-0036-HW9-14. The pipeline then checks scan results specifically for jinja2 and verifies if the project uses a version < 3.1.3. If such a version is present, the pipeline flags the project as having an unpatched dependency. This step ensures the project is updated to jinja2 \u2265 3.1.3 to resolve the vulnerability. The process strictly adheres to the advisory\u2019s affected versions and CVE details, avoiding false positives by confirming the vulnerable version is actively in use. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-14 (s0036_rel id 20087): jinja2 affected < 3.1.3, severity medium. CVE-2024-22195: Cross-site scripting through the xmlattr filter. Fixed in 3.1.3."
