2026-11-12T01:36:12.072-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="eca5262e-cc97-4a2b-89ec-09f4ccd6a522" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (ID 20080), all services using axios are equally critical for patching CVE-2023-45857. The vulnerability affects **axios versions >= 0.8.1 and < 1.6.0** (medium severity), with the fix released in **1.6.0**. Since every service shares the same vulnerable version range and identical severity rating (medium), there is no hierarchy of criticality. All services must be patched to **1.6.0 or higher** to resolve this specific vulnerability. No service should be prioritized over others for this issue\u2014consistent patching across all services is required. Immediate action is needed to update all instances to the fixed version to prevent XSRF-TOKEN cookie disclosure to third-party hosts. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-07 (s0036_rel id 20080): axios affected >= 0.8.1, < 1.6.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-45857: XSRF-TOKEN cookie value disclosed to third-party hosts. Fixed in 1.6.0."
