2026-11-12T01:39:55.780-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="c47959a8-a585-41b3-a54f-ffef74782b7a" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-01, id 20074), **all exposed services using log4j-core >=2.0-beta9 and <2.15.0 are equally critical** for CVE-2021-44228 (Remote code execution via JNDI lookups). The vulnerability has **critical severity** and requires immediate patching to version 2.15.0. Since the facts specify no service-specific exposure details, **prioritize patching any publicly exposed service using the affected log4j-core versions first**\u2014there is no higher criticality distinction among services. All services sharing this vulnerability instance face identical risk. Immediate action is required to update to 2.15.0 to mitigate the critical remote code execution threat. Do not delay patching for any service, as the vulnerability affects all exposed systems using the impacted versions. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-01 (s0036_rel id 20074): log4j-core affected >= 2.0-beta9, < 2.15.0, severity critical. CVE-2021-44228: Remote code execution through JNDI lookups in logged strings (Log4Shell). Fixed in 2.15.0."
2026-11-12T01:39:55.786-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="c47959a8-a585-41b3-a54f-ffef74782b7a" partition=0 offset=339
2026-11-12T01:43:42.951-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="1974734a-b4b8-4072-9b5e-9052b13d5638" partition=0 offset=340 kind="draft"
2026-11-12T01:43:42.956-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="1974734a-b4b8-4072-9b5e-9052b13d5638" status="approved" answer="Until jackson-databind 2.13.2.1 is deployed (fixing CVE-2020-36518), implement these compensating controls per the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-08):  \n\n1. **Validate input data**: Enforce strict input length checks before deserialization to prevent excessively deep JSON structures that cause stack overflow. Monitor for nested objects exceeding safe thresholds (e.g., 100 levels).  \n2. **Whitelist allowed classes**: Configure `ObjectMapper` with a restricted class whitelist using `ObjectMapper.configure()` to permit only trusted classes during deserialization. Avoid dynamic class loading.  \n3. **Avoid untrusted deserialization**: Never use Jackson to deserialize data from untrusted sources (e.g., user-uploaded files, external APIs). For untrusted inputs, reject deserialization entirely or use alternative serialization methods (e.g., JSON parsing without object reconstruction).  \n\nThese measures mitigate the high-severity denial-of-service risk in affected versions (>=2.13.0 <2.13.2.1) until the patch is applied. Ensure all controls are tested in staging environments before deployment. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-08 (s0036_rel id 20081): jackson-databind affected >= 2.13.0, < 2.13.2.1, severity high. CVE-2020-36518: Denial of service through deeply nested JSON (stack overflow). Fixed in 2.13.2.1."
2026-11-12T01:43:42.960-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="1974734a-b4b8-4072-9b5e-9052b13d5638" partition=0 offset=340
2026-11-12T01:46:20.615-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="9463eade-a957-453a-8507-d5f4bc5729b1" partition=0 offset=341 kind="draft"
2026-11-12T01:46:20.620-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="9463eade-a957-453a-8507-d5f4bc5729b1" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-20), the vulnerability CVE-2022-31129 affects moment.js >=2.18.0 <2.29.4 (high severity). **Critical correction**: Log4j JNDI lookups are irrelevant here\u2014this is a moment.js regex DoS issue, not Log4j. Your plan contains an inapplicable step.  \n\n**Valid compensating controls**:  \n1. **Network segmentation**: Isolate moment.js usage from external inputs (e.g., block direct internet access to vulnerable versions via firewalls).  \n2. **Input validation**: Enforce strict date format constraints on all user inputs before passing to moment.js (e.g., use RFC 2822-compliant formats only).  \n3. **Real-time monitoring**: Track unusual date parsing patterns (e.g., excessive regex matches) and alert on abnormal request volumes targeting the vulnerable version.  \n\nDo not disable Log4j JNDI lookups\u2014this addresses a different vulnerability. Prioritize upgrading to moment.js 2.29.4 immediately. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-20 (s0036_rel id 20093): moment affected >= 2.18.0, < 2.29.4, severity high. CVE-2022-31129: Regular expression denial of service when parsing RFC 2822 dates. Fixed in 2.29.4."
2026-11-12T01:46:20.625-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="9463eade-a957-453a-8507-d5f4bc5729b1" partition=0 offset=341
