2026-11-12T01:59:48.412-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="0ac430fc-3fed-405f-b503-df02ce59c157" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-08, id 20081), all services using Jackson Databind versions **>= 2.13.0 but < 2.13.2.1** are vulnerable to CVE-2020-36518 (high severity: denial of service via deeply nested JSON stack overflow). The fix is 2.13.2.1.  \n\nSince all services share the same vulnerable version range and vulnerability impact, **prioritize the service with the highest business criticality and public exposure**. Without specific service details in the facts, the highest-priority service is the one where:  \n1. The service handles the most critical user transactions,  \n2. The service faces the greatest public exposure (e.g., external-facing APIs), or  \n3. The service has the highest risk of outage impact.  \n\nPatch this service first to mitigate the high-severity DoS risk before proceeding to others. All services must update to 2.13.2.1 or later to resolve the vulnerability. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-08 (s0036_rel id 20081): jackson-databind affected >= 2.13.0, < 2.13.2.1, severity high. CVE-2020-36518: Denial of service through deeply nested JSON (stack overflow). Fixed in 2.13.2.1."
