2026-11-12T02:02:12.388-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="77eb89c5-91bf-465c-a2f8-14206b964053" status="approved" answer="Until follow-redirects can be upgraded to version 1.15.6 (fixing CVE-2024-28849), implement these compensating controls:  \n\n1. **Enforce redirect URL whitelisting**: Restrict redirects to predefined, safe domains using the `allow` option in the vulnerable package. This prevents malicious redirects from bypassing authorization checks.  \n2. **Deploy a reverse proxy for redirect validation**: Use a reverse proxy (e.g., Nginx, Apache) to intercept and validate redirect URLs *before* forwarding. Ensure the proxy checks for valid host headers and Proxy-Authorization headers during redirects.  \n3. **Disable automatic redirect following**: Configure the vulnerable package to explicitly skip redirects (`followRedirect: false`) to eliminate the risk of header leakage across hosts.  \n\nThese controls directly mitigate CVE-2024-28849 by preventing unauthorized header propagation during redirects, without requiring package upgrades. They align with the vulnerability\u2019s mechanism\u2014where Proxy-Authorization headers are improperly retained across hosts\u2014ensuring security until the patch is applied. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-21 (s0036_rel id 20094): follow-redirects affected < 1.15.6, severity medium. CVE-2024-28849: Proxy-Authorization header kept across hosts on redirect. Fixed in 1.15.6."
