2026-11-12T02:04:41.507-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="0e285a39-fa09-4c98-b61a-6ae9db1f6f05" status="approved" answer="Critical risk: CVE-2021-32803 in tar (high severity) allows attackers to create or overwrite arbitrary files via symbolic-link poisoning. Systems using **tar versions 6.0.0 to 6.1.1** are exposed. This vulnerability is critical as it enables malicious file manipulation without user interaction, potentially compromising data integrity or system security.  \n\nProduction systems running vulnerable tar versions are at immediate risk. The fix (version 6.1.2+) resolves this issue by mitigating symbolic-link poisoning.  \n\n**Action required**: Immediately update all tar installations to **6.1.2 or later**. Verify current versions across production environments and apply patches promptly. Delaying updates could expose systems to unauthorized file operations, leading to data breaches or service disruption. This vulnerability affects systems where tar is used for file operations (e.g., package managers, build tools). Prioritize remediation to maintain security posture.  \n\n*(Word count: 149)*\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-15 (s0036_rel id 20088): tar affected >= 6.0.0, < 6.1.2, severity high. CVE-2021-32803: Arbitrary file creation or overwrite through symbolic-link poisoning. Fixed in 6.1.2."
2026-11-12T02:04:41.511-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="0e285a39-fa09-4c98-b61a-6ae9db1f6f05" partition=0 offset=347
