2026-11-12T02:07:07.003-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="9f727de6-52f8-4adf-ad94-14f7ae288b14" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-15), CVE-2021-32803 affects all `tar` versions >= 6.0.0 and < 6.1.2 with high severity. This vulnerability allows arbitrary file creation/overwrite via symbolic-link poisoning. Since all services use `tar`, the critical priority is **patching services handling sensitive data or critical system files first**. Services processing user uploads, configuration files, or system binaries are highest risk due to potential data compromise or system instability from malicious file overwrites. \n\nImmediate action: Upgrade all services to `tar` 6.1.2 or later. However, prioritize services where the vulnerability could cause immediate operational impact (e.g., web servers handling user data) over less critical services. Do not delay patching\u2014this high-severity flaw requires urgent remediation to prevent arbitrary file manipulation. Always verify current `tar` versions per service before patching to ensure compliance with the affected range (>=6.0.0 <6.1.2). (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-15 (s0036_rel id 20088): tar affected >= 6.0.0, < 6.1.2, severity high. CVE-2021-32803: Arbitrary file creation or overwrite through symbolic-link poisoning. Fixed in 6.1.2."
