2026-11-12T02:10:13.062-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="5eddd809-45d4-4ecd-a6e3-35c18741e6c1" status="approved" answer="**Risk Note for Management: CVE-2024-28849 in follow-redirects**  \n\nThe open-source package `follow-redirects` (version < 1.15.6) is vulnerable to **CVE-2024-28849** (medium severity). This flaw allows attackers to exploit misconfigured Proxy-Authorization headers across redirects, potentially enabling unauthorized access to protected resources.  \n\n**Impact**: While not critical, this vulnerability could lead to security breaches if systems using `follow-redirects` in production environments handle sensitive headers improperly. Affected versions are widely used in web applications, increasing exposure risk.  \n\n**Action Required**: Immediately upgrade to **version 1.15.6** or later to resolve the issue. Patching is critical to prevent potential exploitation in deployed services. Delaying remediation may expose systems to unauthorized access.  \n\n*Source: s0036_rel advisory ID 20094 (VULN-0036-HW9-21)*  \n\n(Word count: 148)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-21 (s0036_rel id 20094): follow-redirects affected < 1.15.6, severity medium. CVE-2024-28849: Proxy-Authorization header kept across hosts on redirect. Fixed in 1.15.6."
